\pard\keepn\sb300\sa80\b\fs36\cf1 1. Overview\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 The Fluispotter main CPU firmware is a MicroPython application running on the ESP32-S3 Xtensa cores. It implements a cooperative async state machine that drives all user-facing hardware: two peristaltic pumps (AC and blood), a valve, a tape reel, optical sensors, humidity/pressure sensing, RTC timekeeping, WiFi connectivity, and event logging with remote synchronisation. Real-time pump regulation is offloaded entirely to the ULP RISC-V coprocessor (see pump_regulator.py), which runs independently of the main event loop.\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Entry point: main.py calls main(None) which calls MainController.create() then run_safe(controller.run(TimeTable())). All async work runs inside a single asyncio event loop on the main CPU.\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa80\b\fs36\cf1 2. Object Structure\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 MainController inherits from BaseController. The complete object graph is shown below.\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 2.1 BaseController fields\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  event_store --- EventStore: persistent append-only event log (8192-event capacity), synced remotely over WiFi\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  scheduler --- SleepScheduler: manages up to 3 concurrent async sleeps; triggers machine.lightsleep() when all slots are waiting\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  rtc --- RTC: wrapper around MCP79410 real-time clock chip\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  led --- Pin: indication LED (GPIO 44)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  reed --- Button: magnetic reed switch (GPIO 5, pull-up)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  power --- Pin: master power rail enable (GPIO 38)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  ac_pump --- ULPACPump: AC pump interface backed by ULP shared variables\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  blood_pump --- ULPBloodPump: blood pump interface backed by ULP shared variables\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  valve --- ValveMotor: peristaltic valve with open/close hall switches\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  tape_reel --- TapeReel: tape advancement motor\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  tape_receivers --- TapeReceivers: spot and line optical sensors for tape\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  fluid_receivers --- FluidReceivers: AC and blood fluid optical sensors\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  humidity --- HumiditySensor: SHT4X temperature/humidity\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  pressure --- PressureSensor: ADC-based pressure reading\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  state --- int: current state machine state constant\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _tasks --- TaskList: manages background async tasks with cancel-on-exit\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _on_cleanup --- EventListeners: zero-arg callbacks fired on run() exit\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 2.2 MainController-specific fields\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  time_table --- TimeTable: sampling schedule (set at run() call time)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  blood_pump_revolutions --- int: cumulative revolution count for the session\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  ac_pump_revolutions --- int: cumulative revolution count for the session\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _wireless_station_credentials --- WirelessCredentials: cached SSID/BSSID/key from last scan\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _wireless_station --- WirelessNetworkStation: active WiFi connection (None when disconnected)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _fluid_sampling --- Task: continuous fluid sensor sampling coroutine (500 ms interval)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _ac_pump_cycle --- Task: AC pump regulation cycle background task\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _blood_pump_cycle --- Task: blood pump regulation cycle background task\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _blood_pump_cycle_state --- int: ACTIVE | IDLE | SUSPENDED\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _blood_pump_cycle_lock --- Lock: asyncio lock coordinating SAMPLE_BLOOD vs normal cycle\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _blood_pump_sample_history --- deque(maxlen=7): timestamps of last 7 hall switch firings\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 2.3 ULP coprocessor ownership note\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 After ULPPumpRegulator.start() is called during create(), the ULP RISC-V core owns the following resources exclusively and they must NOT be accessed by the main CPU:\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  GPIO 1 (SDA) and GPIO 2 (SCL) --- routed to the RTC I2C peripheral\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  DAC7574 I2C-0 bus --- all writes to DAC channels 0, 1, 3 go through the ULP\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  All pump encoder and enable GPIOs (see ulp/main.c for the full list)\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa80\b\fs36\cf1 3. Startup Sequence --- BaseController.create()\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 create() is a classmethod on BaseController (inherited by MainController). It runs synchronously during program startup before the asyncio loop begins. The steps below are in order of execution.\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 1 --- I2C buses\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  I2C-1: SDA GPIO 39, SCL GPIO 40, 10 kHz --- used for main sensor bus (RTC, VEML, SHT4X)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  I2C-0: SDA GPIO 1,  SCL GPIO 2,  10 kHz --- initially used for DAC7574; handed to ULP at Step 5\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 After Step 5, I2C-0 must not be used directly by the main CPU for DAC pump channels (0, 1, 3).\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 2 --- GPIO pins\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  GPIO 44 --- indication LED (output, initial low)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  GPIO 5  --- reed switch (input, pull-up)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  GPIO 38 --- master power rail (output, initial high)\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 3 --- Peripheral sensors\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  MCP79410 real-time clock --- on I2C-1\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  DAC7574 quad DAC --- on I2C-0 at address 0x4C\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  VEML6035 spot sensor --- on I2C-1 at address 0x48\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  VEML6035 line sensor --- on I2C-1 at address 0x3A\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  SHT4X humidity/temperature --- on I2C-1\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 4 --- Core objects\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  RTC wrapper around MCP79410\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  EventStore: 8192-event capacity, opened from flash (events.db / events.db.index)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Device: HTTP client pointed at http://fluispotter.internal/synchronize\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  SleepScheduler: 3-slot capacity, sleeps via machine.lightsleep\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 5 --- ULP RISC-V pump regulator (critical)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 This step initialises the RISC-V coprocessor. On completion, pump control is entirely owned by the ULP and the main CPU uses shared RTC memory variables to communicate.\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Instantiate ULPPumpRegulator(binary_path="/pump_regulator.bin", sda_gpio=1, scl_gpio=2, clk_hz=100000)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _init_rtc_i2c(): configure RTC I2C peripheral, route GPIO 1/2 to RTC I2C mux (function 3), enable internal pull-ups\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  _load_and_start(): read binary from flash -> write word-by-word to RTC slow memory at 0x50000000 -> zero .bss region (offset 6916..8176) -> RVULP().reset() + RVULP().run()\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Poll machine.mem32[INITIALIZED] until non-zero (up to 5 s timeout); raises RuntimeError on timeout\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Returns ac (ULPACPump) and bp (ULPBloodPump) objects backed by shared RTC memory variables\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 6 --- Actuators and tape/fluid sensors\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  ValveMotor: enable/direction pins + open and close hall switches\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  TapeReel: enable pin\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  TapeReceivers: spot and line VEML light sensors with emitter pins\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  FluidReceivers: AC and blood fluid presence sensors\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 7 --- Environmental sensors\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  HumiditySensor: SHT4X on I2C-1\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  PressureSensor: raw ADC read\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 Step 8 --- Construction\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 All objects are passed to the MainController constructor, which stores them as instance attributes. create() returns the fully-initialised controller instance.\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa80\b\fs36\cf1 4. Async State Machine\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 MainController implements a linear cooperative state machine. run() dispatches to handler functions stored in the class-level states dict. Each handler is an async function that does work, then returns the next state constant (or a tuple of (next_state, *args) to pass arguments to the next handler).\par
