\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 4.3 Per-state detail\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 INITIAL (1)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Entry: closes valve. Attempts to deserialise saved state from flash (blood_pump_revolutions, ac_pump_revolutions, time_table.index, time_table.started_at). If a valid session is found, establishes WiFi, syncs RTC via NTP, restarts any active pump cycles, and transitions directly to SESSION (with advance_time_table=False). If the saved state was the FINISH state, transitions to FINISH. If no saved state is found, transitions to AWAIT_CALIBRATION.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 AWAIT_CALIBRATION (2)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Scans for a WiFi access point whose SSID matches "Fluispotter RPi". On success, connects and waits up to 60 s for device.acquired_at to be set by the server. Enters a command polling loop: blinks LED, calls synchronise(), and checks for incoming commands. PREPARE_SESSION -> CALIBRATION. MAINTAIN_ANTICOAGULANT_PUMP -> AC_PUMP_UPKEEP. PURGE_CATHETER: runs blood pump briefly, then loops back to AWAIT_CALIBRATION.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 AC_PUMP_UPKEEP (3)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Periodically (every 5 minutes) drives the AC pump 30 degrees to prevent coagulation in the anticoagulant line. Between upkeep cycles the device calls machine.lightsleep(10 s). On each wake it checks the reed switch; if pressed, transitions to AWAIT_CALIBRATION.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 CALIBRATION (4)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Performs hardware calibration: cycles valve open then closed, advances tape reel, and drives the blood pump to its park position (hall-switch detected). No user input required. Transitions immediately to AWAIT_ANTICOAGULANT_BAG on completion.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 AWAIT_ANTICOAGULANT_BAG (5)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Opens valve. Blinks LED (2-pulse pattern) to indicate waiting. Polls for the ANTICOAGULANT_BAG_PUNCTURED command from the server, then transitions to ANTICOAGULANT_BAG.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 ANTICOAGULANT_BAG (6)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Starts fluid sensor sampling at 500 ms intervals. Registers AC pump hall-switch event handler. Runs AC pump at fast speed (7 s/rev) with PID regulation. Waits for the ANTICOAGULANT_PRIMED command or a pump monitor timeout, then transitions to AWAIT_CATHETER.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 AWAIT_CATHETER (7)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Closes valve. Starts the AC pump cycle background task (medium speed). Blinks LED (4-pulse pattern). Polls for CATHETER_INSERTED command, then transitions to CATHETER.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 CATHETER (8)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Registers blood pump hall-switch event handler. Runs blood pump at normal speed with PID regulation. Waits for the BLOOD_PRIMED command from the server, then transitions to AWAIT_SESSION.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 AWAIT_SESSION (9)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Starts the blood pump cycle background task. Blinks LED (6-pulse pattern). Stops fluid sampling if blood pump cycle is not yet active. Disconnects WiFi to conserve power. Waits for START_SESSION command. On receipt: starts time_table at current RTC time, then transitions to SESSION.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 SESSION (10)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Main operational loop. Accepts optional advance_time_table argument (bool). If time_table has pending samples: advances (or peeks) the schedule entry, connects WiFi, syncs event store with server, handles any pending commands, then calculates sleep time until the next sample deadline minus a 2-minute preparation buffer. Calls SleepScheduler.sleep_ms() which may trigger machine.lightsleep() until the deadline. When the deadline arrives, transitions to SAMPLE_BLOOD. If no samples remain, syncs once more and transitions to FINISH.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 SAMPLE_BLOOD (11)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Acquires the blood pump cycle lock, suspending any active background regulation. Waits for the blood pump hall switch to fire, accumulating up to 7 timestamps in a deque. Once the oldest timestamp is at or past the scheduled sample time, calls _collect_blood_sample() N times per the schedule entry. After collection, releases the lock, resumes the blood pump cycle, and transitions back to SESSION with advance_time_table=True.\par
\pard\keepn\sb160\sa40\b\fs24\cf2 FINISH (12)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Session complete. Enters an indefinite 10-minute sleep loop. No further transitions are defined; the device waits to be powered off or reset externally.\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa80\b\fs36\cf1 5. run() and run_safe() Mechanics\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 5.1 BaseController.run()\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 run() is an async method. It sets the initial state, starts a background _wait_for_reed_on() task (which monitors the reed switch and cleanly shuts down all tasks when pressed), then enters the dispatch loop:\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Look up handler: fn = self.states[self.state]\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Await handler: result = await fn(self, *args)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Unpack result: if tuple, first element is next state, rest are args; else just next state\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Set self.state = next_state and loop\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 The finally block always runs on exit (normal or exception): cancels all background tasks, then fires all _on_cleanup listeners.\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 5.2 MainController.run()\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Overrides BaseController.run(). Accepts a TimeTable argument (set at call time) and passes initial_state through. Wraps the super() call: on any exception, appends an error event to the event store (with traceback), attempts a final remote sync over WiFi if credentials are available, then re-raises.\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 5.3 run_safe()\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Top-level wrapper called from main(). Creates an asyncio task, runs it to completion, and handles errors:\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  KeyboardInterrupt: silently absorbed (allows clean Ctrl+C from REPL)\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Any other BaseException: logged to fatal-error.txt, then enters a 500 ms LED blink loop\par
\pard\li360\fi-200\sa50\fs22 \bullet  Reed-switch reset: if the reed switch is held for >= 2 consecutive 500 ms checks during error blink, machine.reset() is called\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 run_safe() always calls asyncio.new_event_loop() in the finally block to reset the event loop for potential re-entry (e.g. from REPL).\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa80\b\fs36\cf1 6. Key Supporting Classes\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 SleepScheduler\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Manages a fixed pool of concurrent async sleeps (default capacity 3). Each caller awaits scheduler.sleep_ms(duration_ms), which creates an asyncio.Event and records the deadline. When the pool is full, the scheduler determines the soonest deadline, calls machine.lightsleep(delta_ms), then signals all events whose deadlines have passed. This allows the whole device to enter lightsleep while multiple coroutines are waiting for different intervals.\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 TimeTable\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Stores the sampling schedule as a list of (delta_minutes, sample_count) entries. start(now_ms) records when the session began. peek() returns the absolute timestamp and sample count for the current entry; next() advances the index. any_pending is true while entries remain. Serialised to flash as a compact binary sequence (ushort minutes, ubyte samples per entry) alongside the current index and started_at, enabling session recovery across power cycles.\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 EventStore / Device\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 EventStore is a persistent append-only log backed by two flash files (events.db for payloads, events.db.index for offsets) with a maximum of 8192 events. It delegates remote synchronisation to a Device object, which POSTs to http://fluispotter.internal/synchronize over WiFi. The server responds with pending commands and settings (including a new TimeTable). The Device also exposes acquired_at (set by the server when the device is claimed) and settings.commands (list of pending command strings).\par
\pard\keepn\sb200\sa60\b\fs28\cf1 ULPPumpRegulator\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 Loads and starts the ULP RISC-V coprocessor binary (/pump_regulator.bin). After start(), the coprocessor runs the full pump regulation loop independently: PID speed control, dosing, parking, encoder sampling, and DAC7574 I2C writes. The main CPU communicates via shared uint32_t variables in RTC slow memory (addresses defined in fluispotter/variables.py). ac and bp attributes provide the ULPACPump and ULPBloodPump objects whose API mirrors the original PumpMotor / BloodPumpMotor classes used elsewhere in the codebase.\par
\pard\sa60\par
